{
  "name": "Reframe with Elemental Inference",
  "description": "Manual-trigger pipeline that reframes a video (or a selected video segment) to a vertical aspect ratio using AWS Elemental Inference smart cropping, then polls for completion. The reframed output is saved as a 'smartcrop' derived representation of the source asset. The manual trigger has 'Per Segment Execution' enabled so it can be launched on individual segments (AI or user markers) from the asset detail page, and on selected assets/segments from the bin. Choose the target aspect ratio (default 9:16) on the Video Reframe node. A Download Collector node on the success branch marks the reframed rendition as the pipeline's deliverable, so submitting a selection with 'package outputs for download' zips exactly those renditions — nothing else the asset happens to carry.",
